+## Using a service (for agents — read this before probing `--help`)
+
+Read `docs/services/XX-<name>.md` for a command group the FIRST time you use
+it in a session, instead of walking `copilot <group> --help` and every
+subcommand's own `--help` to reconstruct the grammar. This is the fix for a
+measured, falsified claim: `tools/cse-bench/output/bench_mcp_twin-latest.json`
+(run 20260712T175500Z, `copilot-control-tower`) found CLI Copilot's net
+token advantage over its two direct MCP-server twins (`crm`/nocodb-mcp,
+`db`/postgresql-mcp) is **negative** under probe-everything grammar cost
+(crm -780, db -1894 tokens vs the MCP twin) and only turns positive for
+`crm` (+1238) when the shipped prose doc is read up front instead. The
+`docs/services/*.md` files already exist for every service — reading the
+short reference doc first is cheaper than reconstructing the grammar by
+probing, and it is what makes the CLI's "one grammar instead of a bespoke
+MCP schema per service" claim actually true in practice, not just in
+principle.
